Lachlan, the results are not what anyone expected. Fourteen in-situ probes =
read between 71 and 74 percent relative humidity, well under the 85 percent=
 threshold, with no meaningful difference between the affected band and the=
 control locations. The slab is dry and has been dry.<br />
<br />
The epoxy is in good condition. Two cores show a continuous film at the spe=
cified thickness with no pinholing, and pull-off adhesion came back at 385 =
and 402 pounds per square inch, both above the acceptance criterion. The mo=
isture mitigation system specified in Section 09 05 61 was installed correc=
tly on this job and it is doing exactly what it was designed to do.<br />
<br />
That leaves the question of where the water is coming from, and the answer =
is not underneath. The moisture pattern is worst at the top of the plank se=
ams and the ceiling tile above the corridor at grid F-7 is stained and sagg=
ing. You need a mechanical investigation, not a flooring one.